  "proof_route": [
    "exists_cover_of_hausdorffMeasure_eq_zero: read countable small-diameter covers of small total (d+1)-cost off the infimum formula Measure.hausdorffMeasure_apply; Mathlib's Nonempty guard keeps an empty piece at cost 0 even for d = 0",
    "exists_levelSlab: each cover piece meeting N gets an explicit closed interval of length at most 2 K diam around u of one of its N-points; the Lipschitz estimate compares only points of N; pieces disjoint from N get the empty interval",
    "measurable majorant: a tsum of constant-times-indicator functions, measurable by ENNReal.tsum_eq_iSup_sum and measurability of finite sums",
    "pointwise bound: Measure.hausdorffMeasure_le_liminf_tsum indexed by the subtype {i // t in slab i}; the subtype is required because an empty piece would contribute 0 ^ (0 : R) = 1 for d = 0",
    "integral bound: lintegral_tsum and lintegral_indicator_const give at most 2 K (k+1)^-1; K = 0 needs no branch because every interval is then a single point",
    "Fatou (lintegral_liminf_le') on the MEASURABLE majorants, then lintegral_eq_zero_iff on the measurable liminf; no measurability of the slice function is assumed or used",
    "dimension zero: natural subtraction gives surfaceMeasure V = hausdorffNormalized V (finrank R V) = volume via KLS.hausdorffNormalized_finrank_eq_volume, and monotonicity closes every level; the zero-dimensional fibre measure is NOT treated as the zero measure (the client computes surfaceMeasure univ = 1 there)",
    "positive dimension: Analysis.hausdorffMeasure_finrank_eq_smul_volume turns volume N = 0 into muH[n] N = 0, and ((n-1 : N) : R) + 1 = n needs 1 <= n, so the dimension split is necessary"
  ],
  "not_proved": [
    "L1 with a constant: the Eilenberg measurable majorant with right-hand side C K volume S; only the null special case is proved and no constant C is exhibited",
    "L3 compact-fibre Hausdorff measurability and the open-cover content limit bridge to mkMetric'",
    "L4 Borel-set fibre a.e. measurability",
    "L5 measurable-weight fibre measurability",
    "Analysis.aemeasurable_lintegral_levelSet",
    "Analysis.lintegral_enorm_gradient_mul_eq_lintegral_levelSet",
    "Isoperimetry.lintegral_enorm_gradient_mul_eq_lintegral_levelSet",
    "sharp C^(finrank) Analysis.sard (no downstream consumer) and Analysis.ae_forall_fderiv_ne_zero, both still carrying sorryAx",
    "smoothConstant_le_minkowskiConstant",
    "smoothConstant_mul_lintegral_min_superlevel_le",
    "equality of the two Cheeger constants",
    "L6/L6a/L7 Whitney extension and exact C1 pieces; L8-L12"
